# .trellis/config.yml — Trellis project configuration
#
# This file lets you customize how `trellis update` handles merge conflicts
# on a per-file basis.
#
# By default, certain files (like CLAUDE.md) use a "union" merge strategy
# that keeps both your changes and template updates. You can override this
# behavior here.
#
# Available strategies:
#   union   — Keep both sides of conflicting hunks (good for prose files)
#   theirs  — Prefer template version for conflicting hunks
#   ours    — Prefer local version for conflicting hunks
#   normal  — No automatic resolution; produce conflict markers
#
# Example:
#   mergePolicy:
#     union:
#       - CLAUDE.md
#       - README.md
#     theirs:
#       - package.json
#     normal:
#       - trellis.config.ts
#
# Notes:
#   - CLI flags (--theirs, --ours, --none) override these settings
#   - If mergePolicy is present (even empty), it replaces the built-in defaults
#   - To keep built-in defaults, either omit mergePolicy or delete this file
